            <ArticleTitle>Patients' knowledge of pain agreements.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-46</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000456395.85285.64</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">This study was conducted to determine patients' knowledge of pain agreements.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Descriptive quantitative survey design. A 28-item questionnaire regarding patients' knowledge of pain agreements was distributed to pain management office patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Participants (N = 76) scored 30%-100% (mean 80%) on knowledge of 10 pain agreement items.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Patients demonstrated moderate knowledge of terms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
